# Interview Questions

## What is a Constraint?

A constraint is a rule that ensures valid and consistent data is stored in a database.

---

## Difference between PRIMARY KEY and UNIQUE

| PRIMARY KEY | UNIQUE |
|--------------|---------|
| Cannot contain NULL | Allows one NULL (MySQL) |
| No duplicate values | No duplicate values |
| Only one per table | Multiple UNIQUE constraints allowed |

---

## Difference between PRIMARY KEY and FOREIGN KEY

| PRIMARY KEY | FOREIGN KEY |
|--------------|-------------|
| Uniquely identifies records | Creates relationship between tables |
| Cannot be NULL | Can be NULL (unless restricted) |
| One per table | Multiple allowed |

---

## Difference between NOT NULL and CHECK

| NOT NULL | CHECK |
|-----------|--------|
| Prevents NULL values | Restricts values using a condition |

---

